Inspired by my problems when trying out <Hyperlink href="https://evilmartians.com/chronicles/stop-writing-rules-in-agents-md-use-agent-hooks-and-nano-staged-instead">this setup from evilmartians</Hyperlink>.

typos is a tool specifically made for Claude Code (or GitHub copilot) PostToolUse hook that lints and formats a single edited file without touching
git — reusing a repo's existing .nano-staged.json config, safe under concurrent agent calls, and returning failures as blocking feedback so the agent sees the error and self-corrects.

